          ],
          "retained": [
            "Read variable-length node records and retain neighbor IDs in contiguous storage with per-node edge ranges.",
            "Build an ID-sorted index ordered by input position, then resolve neighbor IDs once; missing IDs are skipped and duplicate IDs use the first input match.",
            "Precompute each node's selected successor using the original strictly positive, first-maximum rule; iteratively cache path sums and print query tokens in original order."
          ]
